  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan entered an unmanned purple-sand space from a yaksha octopus cave and left by the same route.",
      "chapters": [
        934
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Snowy Mountain blessed land is an example of another multi-layered refinement path Gu formation, using twelve layers.",
      "chapters": [
        936
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_snowy_mountain",
        "sys_gu_formation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Old Ancestor Xue Hu did not build that Snowy Mountain formation himself. He asked Sun Ming Lu, then Northern Plains’ number one formation path Gu Immortal, seven times before Sun Ming Lu agreed. Fang Yuan contrasts that twelve-layer work with the remains under the purple sand, which he deduces have at least thirty layers. Thoughts stored in those remains call Limitless Demon Venerable truly worthy, hold his achievements in rule path unmatched and perhaps never to be bettered, and rank their own author far below him. The stored thoughts take him to be right that death holds life and life holds death, and that the two can trade places. Immortal zombies are treated as stuck between life and death, and his direction is called correct. He is called incredibly talented and only some steps away from success. An immortal zombie’s dead aperture is treated as extremely precious, with many uses.",
      "chapters": [
        937
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_old_ancestor_xue_hu",
        "char_sun_ming_lu",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "sys_immortal_zombie"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The life-and-death immortal aperture revival method, a name Fang Yuan gives the unnamed technique, builds on what Limitless Demon Venerable had worked out. It is far superior to cultivation methods passed down for countless years. The mysterious immortal zombie who invented it stood on Old Immortal Kong Jue’s shoulders and used Limitless Demon Venerable’s accomplishments in rule path together with their own talents.",
      "chapters": [
        939
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "cultivation-concept",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_old_immortal_kong_jue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The demonic sounds inside Crazed Demon Cave are the result of Limitless Demon Venerable’s super Gu formation. The Three Crazed Demon Eccentrics estimate that driving living beings crazy was only a side effect and that his true aim was to change the dao marks in living bodies into brand new ones, and Chu Du calls the cave physical proof of that estimate.",
      "chapters": [
        1176
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "super-gu-formation-effects",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_crazed_demon_cave",
        "sys_super_gu_formation",
        "fac_three_crazed_demon_eccentrics",
        "char_chu_du"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The sounds can make a listener go berserk and transform that listener’s body’s dao marks into all sorts of strange dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        1177
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "super-gu-formation-effects",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Demon Immortal Qi Jue, a rank eight Gu Immortal from the Olden Antiquity Era, fought Limitless Demon Venerable three times, splitting a win, a draw, and a loss, with the first two clashes coming before Limitless Demon Venerable reached rank nine. In the deciding battle, fought after that advance, Limitless Demon Venerable needed nine days and nine nights to beat Qi Jue, then spared him, saying Qi Jue had helped push him to his cultivation level and that without such an enemy he would not have trained so hard. That praise from a Demon Venerable marked Qi Jue’s name in history. The grotto-heaven Qi Jue left at his death still stands.",
      "chapters": [
        1319
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "battles-against-qi-jue",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_demon_immortal_qi_jue",
        "evt_era_olden",
        "loc_qi_jue_grotto_heaven"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Limitless Demon Venerable’s rule path true inheritance is among the collection that passes to Fang Yuan when he completely inherits Shadow Sect.",
      "chapters": [
        1435
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rule-path-inheritance-passes-to-fang-yuan",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_shadow_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He has a flawless face. Heavenly Court Gu Immortals who look into Imperfection Regret Pavilion can only see the sides of two vague figures, one male and one female, resembling him and Star Constellation Immortal Venerable.",
      "chapters": [
        1714
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "loc_imperfection_regret_pavilion",
        "char_star_constellation_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "His silhouette becomes increasingly illusory, with only his eyes still bright and letting out sharp lights.",
      "chapters": [
        1955
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "silhouette",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When the last truthful floating ice breaks down, a vague human shaped ice remains, then becomes lifelike, fills with flesh and blood, and turns into a Gu Immortal.",
      "chapters": [
        2207
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "human-shaped-ice",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He is a normal person’s size. Practice Gu’s light envelops his body and expands him to a ten foot giant.",
      "chapters": [
        2208
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ten-foot-giant",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_practice_gu"
      ]
    }
  ],
